/Title (Mutual Information \(MI\) is a feature selection technique that measures how much information one variable provides about another. In machine learning, it tells us how useful a feature is for predicting the target variable. If knowing the value of a feature greatly reduces the uncertainty about the target, then that feature has high mutual information. If the feature provides no useful information about the target, its mutual information is zero.)
/Dest [52 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 1630 0 R
/Next 1419 0 R
>>
endobj
